---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import release from "../../../data/release.json";

const releaseState = release.release.changelog.status === "released"
  ? "released"
  : "candidate";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Supported devices — Burnished Sky Ahead"
  description="Launch devices and verification evidence for Burnished Sky Ahead."
  current="devices"
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Version {release.product.version}</p>
      <h1>Supported devices</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every {releaseState} target passes its native build and visual family gates. Evidence labels keep physical review distinct from Simulator validation.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="content-grid">
      <aside>{release.devices.length} Connect IQ product IDs</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="device-list">
          {release.devices.map((device) => (
            <article class="device-row">
              <p><strong>{device.name}</strong></p>
              <p class="profile">{device.displayProfile.replace("round-", "").replace("x", " × ")} px</p>
              <p class:list={["evidence", { physical: device.evidence.includes("physical") }]}>{device.evidence}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>Some Connect IQ product IDs map to multiple marketed device names. Simulator validation is product-specific acceptance evidence, not a claim of hands-on physical testing. Forerunner 970 is the AMOLED physical reference and Forerunner 245 Music supplied physical MIP Beta evidence; the new 260 × 260 and 280 × 280 families remain Simulator-validated until field reports arrive.</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Native MIP support spans the listed 240 × 240,
          260 × 260, and 280 × 280 families, including Forerunner 245 Music,
          fēnix 6, vívoactive 4, Enduro 3, and fēnix 7X families. Forerunner 255S,
          Approach S62, and unlisted MIP devices remain unsupported.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
